From 02d08c9bdd8a011c78737d5473b79f1c0aea336a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:41:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(kernel): make STEP pcurves on the solidcore kernel

Move the solidcore pin to 2016386 (#2781) and answer its new Blend
surface in the mesh bound and the mesh deviation. The STEP reader now
takes its missing pcurves from the kernel through the solidcore Trims
seam (solidcore_trims::KernelTrims): each face goes to the kernel as an
open sheet, the kernel makes the trims, and each made pcurve is lifted
onto its surface and refused by name past the edge tolerance.

Add the twisted B-spline flank fixtures of #2780 with their bench rows
and a kernel test that reads the closed solid at 8000 mm3.

UNBUILT: verdicts are pinned at the first build.

Fixes #2781
Refs #917
Refs #2780

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
