From 2770ec2c59e1ac554ceba4d8f820261c49936eea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:53:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(kernel): cap the edge-to-surface gap of kernel
 pcurves

KernelTrims refuses an edge that lies more than 0.01 mm off its face's
surface (MAX_EDGE_GAP_MM), set from the gaps measured on the fixtures
that read (largest 1.2e-6 mm). bspline_discontinuous.step (0.25 mm
steps) is refused by name again, as on main.

The bench reads the sc-tess mesh with the kernel's pcurves too. The
fillet_corner and bar_cross_holes rows say "disagree": truck reads both
as open meshes. step_closed_form.rs pins their exact volumes against a
closed form from the fixture dimensions and against the closed sc-tess
mesh. The twisted_flank_off test pins the observed refusal. The interval
and lift checks move to solidcore_trims/checks.rs (400-line rule).

Refs #2781
Refs #917

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
